  "worked_solution": "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{45},\\,b=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
